tiktok-ai-avatar/public/avatar-video.mp4

# ── Must never enter this repo ────────────────────────────────────────────
# This repo is PUBLIC and GitHub Pages serves `main` as a live site, so
# anything committed here is both world-readable and served. See CLAUDE.md.

# Nested repos with their own remotes (adding one records a broken gitlink,
# not the files — and vedic-numerology holds .env with prod DB + Stripe keys)
vedic-numerology/
llm-council/

# Embeds Apps Script / SheetDB endpoints in its .tsx files — write-capable
# credentials for the CueNique admin portal
cunique-billiards/

# Loose local copy; the live deshanechiro.ca is served from its OWN repo
# (devish6/deshane-chiro). Ignoring it here does not affect that site.
deshane-chiro/

# Personal talking-head source footage — the owner filmed at home. This repo
# is PUBLIC and Pages-served, so raw footage of a person must not be committed.
tiktok-ai-avatar/public/talking/

# Unattended scheduler output. The launchd job (deploy/com.numevix.dailyviral.plist)
# writes stdout/stderr here every day at 18:00 with nobody watching. The daily
# pipeline's own commit is path-scoped so it will never add these itself, but a
# stray `git add -A` would — that exact accident has happened once already in
# this repo — and it would publish run logs and stack traces to a live website.
tiktok-ai-avatar/logs/

# MCP server config. Today it holds one public SSE URL and no secret, but this
# is the file that grows an API key the moment a keyed server is added — and
# the rule above is that nothing bearing a key or endpoint enters a public,
# Pages-served repo. It is per-machine tooling, not part of any project here.
.mcp.json

# Cloned-voice narration. Same reasoning as tiktok-ai-avatar/public/talking/:
# this repo is PUBLIC and Pages-served, and a clean isolated sample of a real
# persons cloned voice is far more useful for misuse than the mixed, compressed
# copy that ends up inside a published reel.
tiktok-ai-avatar/public/reels/

# /brag render output. The skill writes its plan, composition, share copy and a
# rendered brag.mp4 into the project directory it runs in, and video is exactly
# the kind of large binary that has no business in a repo GitHub Pages serves.
# Timestamped runs (brag-output-2026-09-17-143022/) are matched too.
brag-output*/

# V67 typefield render artifacts — the composition HTML is tracked, the render is not.
# 🪤 These patterns must carry the FULL path from the repo root: a pattern containing a
# slash is anchored to the .gitignore's own directory, so "v67-typefield/V67.mp4" silently
# matched nothing and the mp4 went public.
tiktok-ai-avatar/v67-typefield/V67.mp4
tiktok-ai-avatar/v67-typefield/V67-poster.jpg
tiktok-ai-avatar/v67-typefield/frames/
tiktok-ai-avatar/v67-typefield/composition/assets/

# V68 receipt — render output and the copied music bed. Same anchoring rule as
# V67: paths are from the repo root, not the video directory.
tiktok-ai-avatar/v68-receipt/V68.mp4
tiktok-ai-avatar/v68-receipt/V68-poster.jpg
tiktok-ai-avatar/v68-receipt/frames/
tiktok-ai-avatar/v68-receipt/composition/assets/

# V69 departures — render output and the copied music bed (paths from the repo root).
tiktok-ai-avatar/v69-departures/V69.mp4
tiktok-ai-avatar/v69-departures/V69-poster.jpg
tiktok-ai-avatar/v69-departures/frames/
tiktok-ai-avatar/v69-departures/composition/assets/

# V70 steam — render output and the copied music bed (paths from the repo root).
tiktok-ai-avatar/v70-steam/V70.mp4
tiktok-ai-avatar/v70-steam/V70-poster.jpg
tiktok-ai-avatar/v70-steam/frames/
tiktok-ai-avatar/v70-steam/composition/assets/
